# Print-in-place fit proof for the sweetheart-hamster clamshell locket.
# `fitcheck` intersects the two CLOSED halves (folded to assembled) — it must
# render EMPTY: the sagittal parting gap is real, so the two halves clear and
# the locket opens instead of printing welded shut. `fitcheck_neg` forces the
# parting gap NEGATIVE (the halves overlap) and MUST interfere — the mandatory
# negative control proving the empty check can actually fail. The living-hinge
# web is drawn outside these bodies, so it never masks the seam clearance.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
